<section id="faq">
 <h2 class="section-title">Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
 <div class="faq-item">
 <h3>Q1: What is the best time to visit Yulla Kanda?</h3>
 <p>A: The best time to visit is from mid-May to mid-October when the weather is pleasant and the trails are accessible.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="faq-item">
 <h3>Q2: Is prior trekking experience required?</h3>
 <p>A: The Yulla Kanda trek is rated as easy to moderate, making it suitable for beginners with a basic level of physical fitness.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="faq-item">
 <h3>Q3: What gear should I carry for the trek?</h3>
 <p>A: We recommend carrying sturdy trekking shoes, layered warm clothing, a raincoat, and a personal water bottle.</p>
 </div>
 <div class="faq-item">
 <h3>Q4: What kind of accommodation is provided?</h3>
 <p>A: Accommodation includes traditional village homestays and premium alpine tents during the trekking days.</p>
 </div>
</section>

<section id="contact" style="background: #f4f4f4;">
